  "outline": [
    "The four basic shapes first, in the corner: e^x, e^(-x) (minus in front of x flips in the y-axis), -e^x (minus in front of the graph flips in the x-axis), -e^(-x) (both minuses flip twice).",
    "The question (line 0), empty axes at the side. Three steps pinned: shape, asymptote, intercepts — the graph drawn as we go.",
    "Step one, shape: it is the minus sign that matters; there is none, so the shape of e^x (line 1), lit in the question, lifted from the corner onto the axes. The numbers 3 and 2 do not change the shape. On 'only stretch it' the lifted e^x stretches into 3e^(2x), so (0, 3) later lands on the curve.",
    "Step two, asymptote: e^x gets closer and closer to the x-axis, never touches it: y = 0 (line 2), dashed.",
    "Step three, intercepts: sub x = 0 (lines 3, 4): y = 3e^(2(0)) = 3e^0 = 3(1) = 3, mark (0, 3). Sub y = 0 (lines 5, 6): e^(2x) = 0, no solutions — an exponential is never zero — no x-intercept.",
    "Last: the sketch in full — the shape of e^x through (0, 3), above the asymptote y = 0, no x-intercept."
